experimental: add structural OpenAPI schema to Graph and GraphRevision CRDs (#248)

## Summary

- Replace the schemaless `x-kubernetes-preserve-unknown-fields` at the
CRD root with a typed structural OpenAPI schema for both Graph and
GraphRevision CRDs
- Node items require `id` (with regex pattern), type body keywords as
named properties with preserve-unknown-fields for mixed string/map
values, type condition expressions as string arrays, and fully type the
status subresource
- Errors like missing id, invalid id characters, and non-string
readyWhen/includeWhen elements are now caught at API server admission
instead of controller reconcile time
- Update 4 e2e tests that deliberately created invalid Graphs to expect
admission rejection instead of controller-level DeclarationError

## What changed

**Graph CRD** (36 → 195 lines) and **GraphRevision CRD** (39 → 181
lines):

| Field | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| `spec.nodes` | untyped | `required`, array with `maxItems: 128` |
| `node.id` | untyped | `required`, string with pattern
`^[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*$` |
| `node.{template,patch,ref,watch,def,forEach}` | invisible | named
properties with `x-kubernetes-preserve-unknown-fields` |
| `node.{includeWhen,readyWhen,propagateWhen}` | untyped | `array of
string`, `maxItems: 32` |
| `node.lifecycle.apply` | untyped | string with `enum: [Force]` |
| `status.conditions` | untyped | `x-kubernetes-list-type: map` keyed by
`type`, all 5 fields typed |
| `status.topologicalOrder` | untyped | typed `nodes` array +
preserve-unknown-fields for forEach keys |

All fields have descriptions for `kubectl explain`.

## What the CRD can't validate (parser still handles)

- Mutual exclusivity of body keywords (CRD CEL can't reference
`x-kubernetes-preserve-unknown-fields` properties)
- Unique node IDs (O(n²) CEL rule exceeds cost budget with unknown-field
items)
- Per-keyword shape rules (template requires apiVersion+kind, patch
requires metadata.name, etc.)
